1
00:01:36,210 --> 00:01:40,050
[River of No Return]

2
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:43,000
[Episode 10: Cricket Fighting]

3
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:48,729
♪ Star-lit halls of splendor rise ♪

4
00:01:48,750 --> 00:02:04,010
♪ All earthly riches gathered inside ♪

5
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,340
Your Highness,

6
00:02:05,510 --> 00:02:06,830
you are revered by all the people.

7
00:02:06,830 --> 00:02:18,300
♪ Lend me a moonbeam, bright as jade ♪

8
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,590
I would like...

9
00:02:09,190 --> 00:02:10,850
to ask for a small favor today.

10
00:02:12,030 --> 00:02:13,310
Could Your Highness

11
00:02:14,030 --> 00:02:15,830
bestow a name upon this banquet?

12
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,280
That way,

13
00:02:17,710 --> 00:02:18,630
even years from now,

14
00:02:18,329 --> 00:02:26,040
♪ To light Yangzhou
through ages of decay ♪

15
00:02:19,270 --> 00:02:21,020
it'll be a cherished family story

16
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:22,950
passed down through generations.

17
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:35,210
Is this fried rice?

18
00:02:35,210 --> 00:02:36,340
Yes, Your Highness.

19
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,520
I've heard

20
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:41,300
that the boatmen and laborers

21
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:42,530
working along the canal

22
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:44,750
eat fried rice most of the time.

23
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:46,110
I'd like to try some.

24
00:03:24,590 --> 00:03:25,800
When Censor Guo

25
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:27,800
spoke of you

26
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:29,070
earlier,

27
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:32,290
he mentioned He Zeng's legendary feasts.

28
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:34,920
They say the canal merchants of Yangzhou

29
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:36,270
are rich beyond imagination.

30
00:03:36,270 --> 00:03:37,329
I dare not say that.

31
00:03:37,930 --> 00:03:39,079
As I see it,

32
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:40,400
Wang Ji,

33
00:03:41,130 --> 00:03:43,190
they're just exaggerating.

34
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:45,550
With just these few dishes,

35
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:47,250
you call this a banquet?

36
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:49,650
It's nothing but a pile of gold scraps.

37
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,550
Gold scraps?

38
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:17,899
This...

39
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:21,500
This is the Gold Scraps Banquet
bestowed upon me by the Crown Prince!

40
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,440
Stop eating!

41
00:04:23,610 --> 00:04:25,080
Stop! Do you hear me?

42
00:04:25,150 --> 00:04:26,730
This is my Gold Scraps Banquet!

43
00:04:26,730 --> 00:04:28,120
Stop eating!

44
00:04:28,230 --> 00:04:30,000
This is my Gold Scraps Banquet!

45
00:04:30,450 --> 00:04:31,540
Stop eating!

46
00:04:34,530 --> 00:04:36,060
Word from Beijing has it

47
00:04:36,230 --> 00:04:38,760
that after the capital
is moved back to Jinling,

48
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:41,490
the canal transport system
will remain in place.

49
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:44,680
But if the court is no longer in Beijing,

50
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:47,680
the volume of canal shipments
heading north each year

51
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,400
will naturally decrease over time.

52
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:52,400
I heard the Wang family
is the biggest canal merchant.

53
00:04:53,590 --> 00:04:55,650
At least half the grain shipped north

54
00:04:55,870 --> 00:04:57,130
for the court each year

55
00:04:57,980 --> 00:04:59,710
is transported by your family.

56
00:04:59,730 --> 00:05:00,320
Yes.

57
00:05:01,650 --> 00:05:03,640
If I take this treasure ship

58
00:05:03,910 --> 00:05:05,680
from Yangzhou to Jinling,

59
00:05:06,270 --> 00:05:08,150
my purpose will be obvious.

60
00:05:09,150 --> 00:05:11,200
Please enlighten me, Your Highness.

61
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,440
In my heart,

62
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:14,650
Beijing should remain the capital

63
00:05:14,650 --> 00:05:15,790
of the Ming Empire.

64
00:05:17,510 --> 00:05:19,910
Since Your Highness has spoken so frankly,

65
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:22,180
allow me to speak my mind as well.

66
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:25,640
His Majesty's plan to move the capital
and abolish canal transport

67
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:27,000
is really just using

68
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:29,570
the people's livelihood as an excuse.

69
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:31,330
Many officials in the capital

70
00:05:31,330 --> 00:05:33,790
believe that canal transport
costs too much

71
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:37,340
and places an unbearable burden
on the people of Jiangnan.

72
00:05:37,730 --> 00:05:38,470
Wang Ji,

73
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,380
how dare you criticize His Majesty?

74
00:05:43,210 --> 00:05:44,540
Do you have a death wish?

75
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:47,070
I wouldn't dare.

76
00:05:47,270 --> 00:05:50,150
Canal transport is vital not only
to the defense of the northern frontier,

77
00:05:50,150 --> 00:05:51,230
but also to the livelihood

78
00:05:51,230 --> 00:05:54,220
of hundreds of thousands of laborers
along the canal.

79
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:57,230
All the people of this realm
are subjects of the Ming Empire,

80
00:05:57,230 --> 00:05:59,710
and so are the hundreds of thousands
of laborers

81
00:05:59,710 --> 00:06:01,110
working along the banks.

82
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:03,330
Everything Your Highness has said

83
00:06:03,330 --> 00:06:06,030
revolves around the people's livelihood.

84
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,030
It's just that Yangzhou

85
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:09,620
is so close to Jinling

86
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:11,850
and so far from Beijing.

87
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:30,840
The farther people are

88
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:32,990
from the imperial court,

89
00:06:33,610 --> 00:06:34,640
the bolder

90
00:06:35,590 --> 00:06:36,830
they become.

91
00:06:47,230 --> 00:06:47,760
Daban.

92
00:06:47,930 --> 00:06:48,290
Yes.

93
00:06:48,310 --> 00:06:50,500
Have Shen Lian draft a memorial right now.

94
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:51,230
State that I

95
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:52,990
insist on accepting the treasure ship

96
00:06:52,990 --> 00:06:55,190
offered by Wang Ji, the canal merchant.

97
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:56,060
Your Highness,

98
00:06:56,150 --> 00:06:57,909
please think this through.

99
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:02,860
Who said you could smile now?

100
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,470
I'd like to see

101
00:07:08,210 --> 00:07:09,770
who dares to be the first to jump out

102
00:07:09,770 --> 00:07:11,700
and talk about court regulations.

103
00:07:11,830 --> 00:07:13,030
Regulations are made by men.

104
00:07:13,030 --> 00:07:13,580
Open the door!

105
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:14,680
We can ignore them,

106
00:07:14,930 --> 00:07:15,680
but...

107
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:16,820
Too slowly.

108
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:20,620
But I'm afraid this will put Your Highness
in a difficult situation.

109
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:23,390
Thank you for your grace, Your Highness.

110
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:36,560
It's all thanks to him

111
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:40,880
that I have come to this point.

112
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:44,650
Thank you.

113
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,600
Congratulations, Master Wang.

114
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:48,830
Congratulations.

115
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:49,760
Congratulations.

116
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,880
Thank you.

117
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:53,880
Thank you.

118
00:07:59,110 --> 00:08:00,440
Distinguished guests,

119
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:01,430
please look.

120
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:08,060
♪ Behind grand gates, feasts never cease ♪

121
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:03,460
[Gold Scraps Banquet]

122
00:08:03,590 --> 00:08:04,880
Gold Scraps Banquet?

123
00:08:05,210 --> 00:08:07,500
Master Wang, may your business prosper.

124
00:08:07,730 --> 00:08:08,440
Thank you.

125
00:08:09,150 --> 00:08:09,850
Thank you.

126
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:12,130
May your business boom.

127
00:08:11,550 --> 00:08:27,570
♪ By the river,
plain meals are hard to come by ♪

128
00:08:12,230 --> 00:08:13,270
Distinguished guests,

129
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:14,530
everyone who's here today

130
00:08:14,530 --> 00:08:16,190
is a friend of the Wang family.

131
00:08:16,390 --> 00:08:18,620
The Crown Prince
bestowed the Gold Scraps Banquet

132
00:08:18,620 --> 00:08:19,830
upon our Wang family,

133
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:24,160
[Wang Da, Steward of Wang's Mansion]

134
00:08:21,330 --> 00:08:23,680
but our master
doesn't want to enjoy it alone.

135
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:27,810
He will host another banquet
at one of the finest restaurants in Yangzhou,

136
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:29,010
with the same dishes

137
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:30,390
and the same spread.

138
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:37,470
♪ In painted halls, silk robes shine ♪

139
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:33,200
We hope you'll all do us the honor
of attending.

140
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,730
Alright. Alright.

141
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,320
Thank you.

142
00:08:36,830 --> 00:08:38,710
Come on, sit down and drink.

143
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:48,990
♪ On these shores, rags offer no warmth ♪

144
00:08:39,830 --> 00:08:40,659
Alright.

145
00:08:41,419 --> 00:08:41,990
Come on.

146
00:08:42,590 --> 00:08:43,440
Steward Wang,

147
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:46,640
the treasure ship Master Wang offered
to the Crown Prince has been blown up.

148
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:47,640
This could easily

149
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:49,420
be construed as treason.

150
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:51,470
And yet you're throwing banquets and...

151
00:08:51,470 --> 00:08:52,180
Lord Zhang.

152
00:08:52,630 --> 00:08:54,030
If you had such concerns,

153
00:08:54,490 --> 00:09:10,040
♪ In manicured gardens, pavilions abound ♪

154
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:58,320
what gave you the courage
to step through the Wang family's door?

155
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:00,110
A few days ago,

156
00:09:00,510 --> 00:09:02,110
I wouldn't have dared come here

157
00:09:02,110 --> 00:09:03,030
even if I had a hundred times the courage.

158
00:09:03,030 --> 00:09:04,170
However...

159
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:08,300
So, whether you attend this banquet
or not,

160
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:10,230
the answer is already in your heart.

161
00:09:10,230 --> 00:09:11,480
Since you've come,

162
00:09:10,310 --> 00:09:29,560
♪ Who cares for the poor
with no roof over their heads? ♪

163
00:09:11,990 --> 00:09:14,160
the Wang family will remember it.

164
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:17,990
I'm not a fool.

165
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:20,200
Master Wang just wants to see

166
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:22,440
who is on his ship, right?

167
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:24,590
Well then.

168
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:26,320
He gets his reassurance,

169
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:28,060
and I get my peace of mind.

170
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:29,800
Please keep drinking.

171
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:30,980
Congratulations.

172
00:09:40,370 --> 00:09:40,990
Master.

173
00:09:41,730 --> 00:09:42,930
What did they all say?

174
00:09:43,130 --> 00:09:44,390
Most had things to say,

175
00:09:44,630 --> 00:09:45,810
but were afraid to be too direct.

176
00:09:45,810 --> 00:09:47,320
They're using the celebration as an excuse

177
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,400
to sound us out.

178
00:09:49,010 --> 00:09:51,330
Quite a few were talking about things like

179
00:09:51,330 --> 00:09:52,830
the bombing of the treasure ship

180
00:09:52,830 --> 00:09:54,290
and the charge of treason.

181
00:09:54,790 --> 00:09:55,480
But now that

182
00:09:55,510 --> 00:09:57,640
things have been quiet for a day or two,

183
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:00,020
they've all started showing up.

184
00:10:01,410 --> 00:10:02,030
Master,

185
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,360
from Jinling's garrison yamen

186
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:05,800
to the Canal Transport Office,

187
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:06,990
which of them hasn't been kept afloat

188
00:10:06,990 --> 00:10:08,390
with our family's money?

189
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:10,230
If anything happens to the Wang family,

190
00:10:10,230 --> 00:10:12,290
none of them will get away unscathed.

191
00:10:12,970 --> 00:10:13,830
These days,

192
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:16,560
no one wants to be treated
like an outsider.

193
00:10:17,630 --> 00:10:19,560
Everyone who came today is shrewd.

194
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,690
Now that you're safe and sound,

195
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:24,200
they'll all be counting on you

196
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,510
for future business.

197
00:10:25,870 --> 00:10:27,470
If they didn't show up today,

198
00:10:27,490 --> 00:10:29,020
they'd risk offending you.

199
00:10:32,710 --> 00:10:33,590
So...

200
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:38,730
whether they came or stayed away,

201
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:41,110
they were taking a gamble.

202
00:10:55,290 --> 00:10:57,510
[Lu Chaihua, Cook]

203
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,040
Today,

204
00:11:10,110 --> 00:11:11,840
it's mung bean sprout wontons.

205
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:14,930
I haven't had these in ages.

206
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:17,900
The Principles of Correct Diet mentions

207
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:19,350
24-solar-term wontons,

208
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:22,620
each corresponding
to one of the 24 solar terms.

209
00:11:22,830 --> 00:11:24,460
With the Summer Solstice approaching,

210
00:11:24,460 --> 00:11:25,400
I added

211
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:27,940
mung bean sprouts
and tender melon shreds to the filling.

212
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:30,600
That's what gives them
their refreshing taste.

213
00:11:30,710 --> 00:11:32,240
After the Summer Solstice,

214
00:11:32,970 --> 00:11:35,080
the days grow shorter
and the nights longer,

215
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,610
as yang wanes and yin waxes.

216
00:11:37,130 --> 00:11:38,680
I have a feeling the world

217
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:40,250
is about to change, too.

218
00:11:41,130 --> 00:11:42,560
I think autumn is lovely.

219
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:46,040
So many delicious things
are only available in autumn.

220
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:46,920
Going with the flow

221
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,650
isn't necessarily a bad thing.

222
00:11:49,230 --> 00:11:51,510
But I may not live to enjoy them.

223
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:57,800
Master,

224
00:11:58,130 --> 00:11:59,460
what exactly happened?

225
00:12:06,060 --> 00:12:07,990
The treasure ship I presented
to the Crown Prince...

226
00:12:07,990 --> 00:12:09,040
Once it exploded,

227
00:12:10,830 --> 00:12:12,830
whether I did it on purpose

228
00:12:12,870 --> 00:12:14,400
or not,

229
00:12:14,850 --> 00:12:16,110
the whole world

230
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:19,350
would see it as an act of treason.

231
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:26,870
Father, hurry up!

232
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:29,800
Hurry!

233
00:12:46,970 --> 00:12:47,630
Doctor Su?

234
00:12:48,130 --> 00:12:49,190
Do you remember me?

235
00:12:49,510 --> 00:12:50,200
You healed my leg.

236
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,230
I do. Yes.

237
00:12:51,470 --> 00:12:52,800
Go ahead with your work.

238
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:54,760
She came back for Lord Guo, right?

239
00:12:54,990 --> 00:12:56,230
Poor thing.

240
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:58,870
They weren't even married yet.

241
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:01,140
[Guo's Mansion]

242
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:03,500
[In Memory of Guo Zhimin]

243
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,350
Master, look.

244
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:16,710
-She's here.
-Who is she?

245
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:18,320
The young master's fiancée.

246
00:13:16,830 --> 00:13:18,810
[Guo Chunzhi, Renowned Confucian Scholar]

247
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:19,040
What?

248
00:13:18,810 --> 00:13:20,790
[of the Region West of the Huai River,
Father of Guo Zhimin]

249
00:13:23,870 --> 00:13:24,680
Su Jingxi,

250
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,320
what are you doing here?

251
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:28,720
I never agreed to your marriage
with my son.

252
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:32,490
There is no need for you
to set foot in Guo's Mansion.

253
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:34,320
Get out.

254
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:35,710
Mr. Guo.

255
00:13:36,580 --> 00:13:38,440
Although Zhimin and I
were not destined to be together,

256
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:40,300
we did know each other, after all.

257
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:42,280
It is only right for me to see him off.

258
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:43,350
See him off?

259
00:13:43,750 --> 00:13:44,320
Fine.

260
00:13:46,310 --> 00:13:47,690
Makes sense.

261
00:13:48,510 --> 00:13:51,110
Sounds like something
the Su family would say.

262
00:13:54,060 --> 00:13:54,780
Kneel.

263
00:13:56,750 --> 00:13:58,440
Didn't you want to be with him?

264
00:14:01,870 --> 00:14:02,800
Jump into a well,

265
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,440
starve yourself,

266
00:14:04,970 --> 00:14:05,970
or hang yourself—

267
00:14:06,330 --> 00:14:07,230
pick one

268
00:14:08,470 --> 00:14:10,080
and go with my son.

269
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:13,320
You didn't share a bed in life,

270
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:15,130
but I guarantee you will

271
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:16,800
share a grave in death.

272
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:20,080
You want to be honored as a chaste martyr?

273
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:22,340
I'll petition His Majesty

274
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:24,480
to build a memorial arch for you.

275
00:14:24,510 --> 00:14:25,470
How about that?

276
00:14:32,610 --> 00:14:33,280
Wait!

277
00:14:33,590 --> 00:14:34,320
Wait!

278
00:14:35,460 --> 00:14:36,110
Wait!

279
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:41,010
Tell me the truth.

280
00:14:43,230 --> 00:14:45,160
How exactly did my son die?

281
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:49,250
Yingtian Prefectural Office
closed the case,

282
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:51,440
saying he died from a collapsed beam
during the earthquake.

283
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:53,490
A collapsed beam during the earthquake?

284
00:14:53,490 --> 00:14:55,220
Only a fool would believe that!

285
00:14:55,630 --> 00:14:57,030
Who can tell me the truth?

286
00:14:58,630 --> 00:15:00,350
My condolences, Mr. Guo.

287
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:06,560
Who can tell me the truth?

288
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:25,080
Wang Ji!

289
00:15:26,830 --> 00:15:27,470
Lord Guo,

290
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:29,230
my condolences.

291
00:15:30,110 --> 00:15:31,370
How dare you come here?

292
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:34,160
How dare you step through
the Guo family's door?

293
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:36,470
Why wouldn't I dare?

294
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:40,390
You can know a person's face,
but not their heart.

295
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:41,960
Our two families

296
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:45,590
had been friends for three generations.

297
00:15:46,590 --> 00:15:49,830
I thought
that my son persuading your family

298
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:52,640
to present a treasure ship
to the Crown Prince

299
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:55,630
would bring honor to both our houses.

300
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:56,180
Yes.

301
00:15:56,210 --> 00:15:57,270
But what did you do?

302
00:15:57,490 --> 00:15:58,360
You had ulterior motives all along!

303
00:15:58,360 --> 00:15:59,290
You actually...

304
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:02,320
dragged my family into a pit of no return!

305
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:02,990
Bastard!

306
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:04,540
I'll beat you to death!

307
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:05,840
Lord Guo, Lord Guo!

308
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:06,800
Don't do this!

309
00:16:38,460 --> 00:16:39,390
Little Xingren.

310
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:40,460
Let me ask you.

311
00:16:40,830 --> 00:16:43,470
How do you plan
to get that letter of passage

312
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:44,830
from that head steward?

313
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:46,700
You don't seriously think

314
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:48,590
he'll just give it to you

315
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:51,510
because you beg him, do you?

316
00:16:52,630 --> 00:16:54,230
We'll appeal to his emotions

317
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:56,010
or his sense of righteousness.

318
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:57,160
That's your plan?

319
00:16:57,380 --> 00:16:59,310
Well, if he won't listen to reason,

320
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,560
we'll just use force.

321
00:17:02,970 --> 00:17:04,160
We'll storm in

322
00:17:05,030 --> 00:17:06,160
and take it from him.

323
00:17:10,839 --> 00:17:13,839
That's

324
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:15,410
complete nonsense.

325
00:17:15,530 --> 00:17:16,730
Let me put it this way.

326
00:17:17,250 --> 00:17:18,750
Every gambling den

327
00:17:18,970 --> 00:17:20,750
has its own gang of enforcers.

328
00:17:21,119 --> 00:17:24,290
With your amateur fighting skills,
you think you can take them on?

329
00:17:24,290 --> 00:17:25,310
Forget it.

330
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:26,970
And even if you somehow get the letter,

331
00:17:26,970 --> 00:17:28,600
they'll make a huge scene.

332
00:17:28,750 --> 00:17:30,990
Do you think your young master
will still be allowed on the ship?

333
00:17:30,990 --> 00:17:32,990
He'll be stuck on shore all the same.

334
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:39,360
Then tell me.

335
00:17:40,470 --> 00:17:41,600
What do you suggest?

336
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:42,990
What do I suggest?

337
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:47,200
Right now,

338
00:17:47,810 --> 00:17:49,010
there's only one way.

339
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,990
That steward loves gambling, doesn't he?

340
00:17:50,990 --> 00:17:51,660
Then we'll

341
00:17:51,790 --> 00:17:52,950
play fair and square,

342
00:17:52,950 --> 00:17:54,610
win a big sum of money from him,

343
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:57,820
and make him trade the letter of passage
for the money.

344
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,410
You should've said so earlier.

345
00:18:03,340 --> 00:18:05,670
How was I supposed to know
he was a gambler?

346
00:18:05,810 --> 00:18:06,610
Let me ask you.

347
00:18:07,270 --> 00:18:08,710
Which are you good at?

348
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,680
Dice, cricket fighting,

349
00:18:11,010 --> 00:18:11,750
or pai gow?

350
00:18:12,770 --> 00:18:13,400
Me?

351
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,490
How would I know any of that?

352
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:20,440
Then we're doomed.

353
00:18:21,270 --> 00:18:22,280
Nine out of ten playboys are gamblers.

354
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:23,700
Aren't you a notorious playboy

355
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:24,960
in Jinling?

356
00:18:25,810 --> 00:18:27,630
You must have some tricks up your sleeve.

357
00:18:27,630 --> 00:18:28,150
Tell me.

358
00:18:29,510 --> 00:18:30,510
I

359
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,030
value money

360
00:18:32,910 --> 00:18:34,110
more than my own life.

361
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:37,570
I can't stand watching
thousands of taels change hands

362
00:18:37,990 --> 00:18:40,250
in the blink of an eye
at a gambling table.

363
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:44,200
Then what are we even talking about?

364
00:18:50,070 --> 00:18:51,270
I just heard

365
00:18:52,010 --> 00:18:53,070
they're betting on

366
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:56,250
artificially bred crickets
at the gambling den, right?

367
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:39,340
Which one should we bet on?

368
00:19:45,070 --> 00:19:46,000
Let me have a try.

369
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:51,300
That's too much.

370
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:57,000
Open the gate.

371
00:20:04,980 --> 00:20:06,680
♪ The gambling den is loud and packed ♪

372
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:08,700
♪ A crush of bodies, hot as a kiln ♪

373
00:20:08,730 --> 00:20:10,540
♪ Crickets leap into the fray ♪

374
00:20:10,100 --> 00:20:10,960
The match is over.

375
00:20:10,560 --> 00:20:14,020
♪ The crowd pounds the tables,
roaring with laughter ♪

376
00:20:11,030 --> 00:20:11,920
Master Li won.

377
00:20:12,230 --> 00:20:13,600
Well played.

378
00:20:14,230 --> 00:20:15,290
Here's your money.

379
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:18,560
We can really win money doing this.

380
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:19,390
Master Li, here is yours.

381
00:20:19,390 --> 00:20:20,040
Here.

382
00:20:20,310 --> 00:20:21,510
Thank you, Master Li.

383
00:20:23,420 --> 00:20:24,200
Sir.

384
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:27,750
The money we've won

385
00:20:27,930 --> 00:20:29,140
should be enough to buy this cricket,
right?

386
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:29,490
Wait.

387
00:20:29,530 --> 00:20:30,270
Yes.

388
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:31,470
This is my money.

389
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:32,390
You...

390
00:20:32,510 --> 00:20:33,270
Brat.

391
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:35,020
Come on. Old Mule.

392
00:20:35,020 --> 00:20:36,760
You could have bought any cricket you wanted
with that money.

393
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:38,450
Why did you waste it on a lousy one?

394
00:20:38,450 --> 00:20:39,980
I know how to make you money.

395
00:20:40,250 --> 00:20:40,910
Seriously?

396
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:41,920
With this?

397
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:44,500
Don't worry.
I'll win the money back for you.

398
00:20:54,190 --> 00:20:56,060
♪ They bet this way and that,
hoping to strike it rich ♪

399
00:20:56,090 --> 00:20:57,830
♪ Never knowing
the winner's fixed in advance ♪

400
00:20:57,850 --> 00:20:59,840
♪ A pinch of powder slips from a sleeve ♪

401
00:20:59,870 --> 00:21:01,640
♪ From above,
you're just bugs trapped in a jar ♪

402
00:21:01,670 --> 00:21:03,520
♪ They bet this way and that,
hoping to strike it rich ♪

403
00:21:03,540 --> 00:21:05,370
♪ Never knowing
the winner's fixed in advance ♪

404
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:05,960
Come on. It's not enough?

405
00:21:05,390 --> 00:21:07,390
♪ A pinch of powder slips from a sleeve ♪

406
00:21:06,790 --> 00:21:07,550
Give it to him!

407
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:09,420
♪ From above,
you're just bugs trapped in a jar ♪

408
00:21:08,170 --> 00:21:09,070
Do you know anything about this?

409
00:21:09,070 --> 00:21:09,790
Give it to him.

410
00:21:09,790 --> 00:21:11,600
Cricket fighting with artificially bred crickets
is all about matching bets.

411
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:12,660
They placed a bet,

412
00:21:12,660 --> 00:21:13,750
and you matched it with an equal amount.

413
00:21:13,750 --> 00:21:14,660
That was enough.

414
00:21:14,660 --> 00:21:16,070
I'm telling you. If we win, it doubles.

415
00:21:16,070 --> 00:21:17,030
What if we lose?

416
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:18,130
Come on.

417
00:21:18,130 --> 00:21:19,640
You know nothing about this.

418
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:20,700
What are you doing?

419
00:21:23,970 --> 00:21:24,770
Young Master.

420
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:25,850
-Th-This is too much, don't you think?
-The bets have been placed.

421
00:21:25,850 --> 00:21:26,800
Bets are final.

422
00:21:27,270 --> 00:21:28,880
Nobody plays like this!

423
00:21:29,860 --> 00:21:31,070
This is way too much!

424
00:21:32,130 --> 00:21:34,050
I am willing to duel with you.

425
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:36,260
Sir, please open the cricket jar.

426
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:49,710
This bet—

427
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:50,750
I'll take it.

428
00:21:53,700 --> 00:21:54,630
All in?

429
00:21:57,440 --> 00:21:58,050
Please.

430
00:22:02,010 --> 00:22:02,810
Open the gate.

431
00:22:03,460 --> 00:22:04,810
♪ Swaying along, swaying along ♪

432
00:22:04,830 --> 00:22:06,120
♪ Swaying along, swaying along ♪

433
00:22:06,150 --> 00:22:07,650
♪ Swaying along—
what's all the swaying for? ♪

434
00:22:07,830 --> 00:22:10,000
Why is Master Li's Nine-Headed Dragon
afraid to fight?

435
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:10,140
♪ Chasing them down, chasing them down ♪

436
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:11,520
♪ Chasing them down, chasing them down ♪

437
00:22:11,030 --> 00:22:13,120
Why does the Nine-Headed Dragon
keep dodging?

438
00:22:11,540 --> 00:22:13,770
♪ Chasing them down—
what am I chasing for? ♪

439
00:22:14,360 --> 00:22:15,950
♪ Who knows? Who cares about me? ♪

440
00:22:15,970 --> 00:22:17,380
♪ Who knows? Who cares about me? ♪

441
00:22:16,230 --> 00:22:17,230
Stop dodging.

442
00:22:17,460 --> 00:22:18,470
Go bite it!

443
00:22:17,490 --> 00:22:19,190
♪ Who knows where home is? ♪

444
00:22:19,420 --> 00:22:21,230
Didn't they just have a match?

445
00:22:20,010 --> 00:22:21,460
♪ To hell with princes and nobles ♪

446
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,550
Master Li won decisively.

447
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:22,890
♪ To hell with
what the history books say ♪

448
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:24,960
Yeah, this is too weird.

449
00:22:22,910 --> 00:22:24,830
♪ I'm my own guardian angel ♪

450
00:22:26,280 --> 00:22:29,000
♪ Call me crazy, call me a coward ♪

451
00:22:29,030 --> 00:22:30,420
♪ The Qinhuai River breeds fools like me ♪

452
00:22:31,820 --> 00:22:34,660
♪ A knife tucked at my waist,
wine burning in my throat ♪

453
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:36,380
♪ Both feet planted in the mud ♪

454
00:22:35,310 --> 00:22:36,290
See? What did I say?

455
00:22:36,290 --> 00:22:36,840
What did I tell you?

456
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:38,160
The two crickets fought to a draw,

457
00:22:37,450 --> 00:22:40,300
♪ I brave the wind, I hit the ground ♪

458
00:22:38,840 --> 00:22:39,860
but this gentleman

459
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:41,160
clearly has the upper hand.

460
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:42,000
♪ I take the blows head-on,
never crying out in pain ♪

461
00:22:41,530 --> 00:22:43,060
That's called a "hook win."

462
00:22:43,180 --> 00:22:46,220
♪ My life hangs by a thread,
my worries buried in my bones ♪

463
00:22:44,790 --> 00:22:45,400
Mr. Zhang!

464
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:46,360
The Jade Qilin!

465
00:22:46,250 --> 00:22:48,250
♪ Whatever I owe, I'll repay in time ♪

466
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:50,040
♪ Swaying along, swaying along ♪

467
00:22:50,070 --> 00:22:51,360
♪ Swaying along, swaying along ♪

468
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:52,890
♪ Swaying along—
what's all the swaying for? ♪

469
00:22:54,140 --> 00:22:55,380
♪ Chasing them down, chasing them down ♪

470
00:22:55,510 --> 00:22:56,750
♪ Chasing them down, chasing them down ♪

471
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:56,680
Master Fang!

472
00:22:56,770 --> 00:22:59,000
♪ Chasing them down—
what am I chasing for? ♪

473
00:22:56,920 --> 00:22:58,650
The Ever-victorious General!

474
00:22:59,590 --> 00:23:01,180
♪ Who knows? Who cares about me? ♪

475
00:23:01,210 --> 00:23:02,610
♪ Who knows? Who cares about me? ♪

476
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:04,420
♪ Who knows where home is? ♪

477
00:23:05,250 --> 00:23:06,690
♪ To hell with princes and nobles ♪

478
00:23:06,730 --> 00:23:08,120
♪ To hell with
what the history books say ♪

479
00:23:08,150 --> 00:23:10,360
♪ I'm my own guardian angel ♪

480
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:09,920
Master He!

481
00:23:10,270 --> 00:23:11,600
The Eight-Armed Nezha!

482
00:23:34,750 --> 00:23:35,550
Young Master,

483
00:23:35,620 --> 00:23:36,750
we've struck it rich!

484
00:23:36,750 --> 00:23:37,880
You're incredible!

485
00:23:38,010 --> 00:23:39,870
We didn't get to see Steward Wang,

486
00:23:40,070 --> 00:23:41,800
but this trip was well worth it.

487
00:23:42,490 --> 00:23:45,150
Don't worry.
He will definitely come tomorrow.

488
00:23:45,690 --> 00:23:46,320
Old Mule,

489
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:47,370
when you have time,

490
00:23:47,370 --> 00:23:48,500
teach me that trick.

491
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:49,750
If I can do that,

492
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:52,520
I don't even need
to keep being a constable.

493
00:23:54,830 --> 00:23:56,690
Young Master, where are we going?

494
00:23:58,070 --> 00:23:58,730
We'll wait.

495
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:00,380
Wait for Wang to invite us.

496
00:24:01,820 --> 00:24:02,430
Careful!

497
00:24:02,720 --> 00:24:04,520
-No need to help me.
-Be careful!

498
00:24:04,770 --> 00:24:06,230
No need. No need to help me.

499
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:07,680
No need...

500
00:24:09,710 --> 00:24:10,400
Be careful!

501
00:24:15,920 --> 00:24:16,750
Old Mule.

502
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:18,640
Old Mule.

503
00:24:20,340 --> 00:24:21,160
Tell me,

504
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:23,310
what kind of magic did you use

505
00:24:23,750 --> 00:24:25,430
on this Great General?

506
00:24:25,770 --> 00:24:27,030
Let me in on the secret.

507
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:31,070
There's nothing.

508
00:24:31,440 --> 00:24:32,200
Impossible.

509
00:24:36,750 --> 00:24:38,840
Every time before you opened the gate,

510
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:40,440
you fiddled with

511
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:41,640
that little jar.

512
00:24:41,710 --> 00:24:43,440
Don't think I haven't noticed.

513
00:24:43,860 --> 00:24:44,960
What was that little treasure of yours?

514
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:46,960
The eunuchs in the palace in Beijing

515
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:50,140
have to compete in cricket fights
against their masters from time to time.

516
00:24:50,140 --> 00:24:51,470
Afraid of winning

517
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:54,050
and displeasing their masters,

518
00:24:54,050 --> 00:24:56,050
they come up with all sorts of tricks

519
00:24:56,510 --> 00:24:57,800
to keep them happy.

520
00:24:57,820 --> 00:24:58,650
[Peking Spurge]

521
00:25:07,270 --> 00:25:07,750
Come on.

522
00:25:14,360 --> 00:25:16,560
No wonder you are the Crown Prince.

523
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:20,770
Let me tell you,

524
00:25:21,580 --> 00:25:23,860
no matter how fierce
an artificially bred cricket is,

525
00:25:23,860 --> 00:25:24,790
it has its fears,

526
00:25:25,340 --> 00:25:26,340
just like people.

527
00:25:26,740 --> 00:25:27,870
Aren't you the same?

528
00:25:30,270 --> 00:25:31,750
Playing dirty like this,

529
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:34,140
weren't you afraid of
getting your hands chopped off?

530
00:25:34,140 --> 00:25:35,360
I had no other choice.

531
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:36,930
Aren't they still here?

532
00:25:40,340 --> 00:25:42,230
If only I had met you earlier.

533
00:25:43,420 --> 00:25:45,150
If you had taught me this trick,

534
00:25:45,850 --> 00:25:48,450
my father wouldn't have to work
as a constable.

535
00:25:51,860 --> 00:25:53,860
Speaking of working as a constable,

536
00:25:54,270 --> 00:25:55,670
your father was actually

537
00:25:56,230 --> 00:25:57,830
doing quite well in Jinling.

538
00:25:57,970 --> 00:25:59,880
That's true.

539
00:25:59,910 --> 00:26:00,770
Let me tell you,

540
00:26:01,100 --> 00:26:01,710
Old Mule,

541
00:26:02,030 --> 00:26:03,070
I'm not bragging.

542
00:26:03,490 --> 00:26:05,690
Across the entire Southern Zhili area,

543
00:26:06,470 --> 00:26:08,130
I haven't seen a second person

544
00:26:08,190 --> 00:26:10,910
who dares to bear the title of Iron Lion.

545
00:26:14,260 --> 00:26:15,150
Wu Dingyuan,

546
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:18,210
then why is your nickname
Good-for-Nothing?

547
00:26:18,890 --> 00:26:21,420
Does it have anything to do
with your illness?

548
00:26:24,920 --> 00:26:26,320
That's what they all say.

549
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:27,890
When I was young,

550
00:26:28,940 --> 00:26:30,270
I got a strange illness.

551
00:26:31,510 --> 00:26:33,960
My father took me and my sister

552
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:35,620
to Jinling to see a doctor.

553
00:26:37,700 --> 00:26:38,960
The illness was cured,

554
00:26:38,970 --> 00:26:40,970
but it left me with lasting effects.

555
00:26:42,230 --> 00:26:43,660
I not only can't remember anything

556
00:26:43,660 --> 00:26:44,520
from back then,

557
00:26:46,140 --> 00:26:48,810
but I also get a headache
when I see firelight.

558
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:52,990
It's nothing important.

559
00:26:56,340 --> 00:26:57,270
Can I

560
00:26:57,640 --> 00:26:58,700
ask you something?

561
00:26:59,920 --> 00:27:00,550
Go ahead.

562
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:02,570
What kind of person

563
00:27:02,570 --> 00:27:03,640
does your father

564
00:27:03,990 --> 00:27:05,710
want you to be?

565
00:27:08,070 --> 00:27:10,300
I don't need him
to have any expectations of me.

566
00:27:10,300 --> 00:27:11,900
To my imperial grandfather,

567
00:27:12,010 --> 00:27:13,270
I am his good grandson.

568
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:15,400
To my father,

569
00:27:17,140 --> 00:27:18,940
I was born to be the Crown Prince.

570
00:27:21,510 --> 00:27:22,600
People

571
00:27:23,360 --> 00:27:24,600
are just different.

572
00:27:25,510 --> 00:27:26,680
My father

573
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:28,360
wished

574
00:27:28,770 --> 00:27:30,700
I'd been born a good-for-nothing.

575
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:32,940
Let me tell you.

576
00:27:32,940 --> 00:27:34,030
I really believe

577
00:27:34,680 --> 00:27:35,990
there are some things

578
00:27:36,290 --> 00:27:38,920
we're just born to do.

579
00:27:39,760 --> 00:27:42,210
Like being a constable.

580
00:27:42,660 --> 00:27:44,920
I've always felt
I was cut out for the job.

581
00:27:45,310 --> 00:27:45,960
But my father

582
00:27:45,960 --> 00:27:47,440
never let me get involved in cases.

583
00:27:47,440 --> 00:27:49,440
I argued with him, I fought him on it,

584
00:27:49,770 --> 00:27:51,570
but I just couldn't get through to him.

585
00:27:51,570 --> 00:27:52,900
So I just let him have his way

586
00:27:52,900 --> 00:27:54,100
and gave up on myself.

587
00:27:56,960 --> 00:27:58,820
When our fathers are still alive,

588
00:27:58,970 --> 00:28:01,640
we're always looking for ways
to go against them.

589
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:03,370
We'd try to get away with things

590
00:28:04,160 --> 00:28:05,360
and talk back to them.

591
00:28:05,820 --> 00:28:06,540
But now,

592
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:08,050
who knows if we'll get another chance

593
00:28:08,050 --> 00:28:09,360
to talk back to them

594
00:28:09,710 --> 00:28:11,110
or act spoiled with them?

595
00:28:15,840 --> 00:28:16,400
Come on.

596
00:28:16,990 --> 00:28:19,270
Call Steward Wang over here.

597
00:28:20,110 --> 00:28:21,170
I'll get him drunk.

598
00:28:22,390 --> 00:28:24,120
I'll drink him under the table!

599
00:28:24,720 --> 00:28:25,260
I...

600
00:28:26,510 --> 00:28:27,920
Call Steward Wang out.

601
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:29,920
Looks like

602
00:28:30,510 --> 00:28:32,240
he's had quite enough to drink.

603
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:33,550
Tell me,

604
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:35,440
what kind of honor

605
00:28:36,160 --> 00:28:38,290
do you want bestowed upon your father?

606
00:28:40,440 --> 00:28:41,230
An honor?

607
00:28:42,070 --> 00:28:43,310
Did you just say

608
00:28:43,840 --> 00:28:45,470
you were going to honor my father?

609
00:28:45,470 --> 00:28:46,800
Then let me ask you this.

610
00:28:48,140 --> 00:28:50,930
What do you plan to do
for my fellow constables

611
00:28:51,440 --> 00:28:53,180
from the Yingtian Prefectural Office
who lost their lives?

612
00:28:53,180 --> 00:28:54,320
After I return to Beijing,

613
00:28:54,320 --> 00:28:55,790
I'll issue an imperial decree.

614
00:28:55,790 --> 00:28:56,790
Each fallen man

615
00:28:57,050 --> 00:28:58,110
will receive 1,000 taels of silver,

616
00:28:58,110 --> 00:29:00,560
be posthumously granted the title
of Marquis of a Thousand Households,

617
00:29:00,560 --> 00:29:03,290
and have that honor extended
to his descendants.

618
00:29:03,300 --> 00:29:04,960
So should I get down on my knees

619
00:29:05,470 --> 00:29:06,510
right here

620
00:29:06,670 --> 00:29:08,470
and kowtow on behalf of my father

621
00:29:08,750 --> 00:29:10,280
and all my fallen brothers?

622
00:29:10,750 --> 00:29:13,150
Thank you for Your Highness's generosity?

623
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:14,920
What's wrong?

624
00:29:15,960 --> 00:29:17,710
Can't you speak properly
when you're drunk?

625
00:29:17,710 --> 00:29:19,190
This is how I speak!

626
00:29:19,730 --> 00:29:21,070
Do you think

627
00:29:21,790 --> 00:29:22,960
with your lousy reward,

628
00:29:22,960 --> 00:29:24,360
they died a worthy death?

629
00:29:26,180 --> 00:29:27,510
If you are happy,

630
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:29,470
you might give out more rewards.

631
00:29:29,470 --> 00:29:30,920
If you are unhappy,

632
00:29:31,100 --> 00:29:32,100
you give out less,

633
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:33,940
or even nothing at all.

634
00:29:34,360 --> 00:29:35,560
Is that what you mean?

635
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:39,440
Of course not.

636
00:29:40,360 --> 00:29:41,670
Rewards cannot compensate for lives.

637
00:29:41,670 --> 00:29:43,200
I have a guilty conscience,

638
00:29:43,380 --> 00:29:45,150
but this is all I can do.

639
00:29:46,680 --> 00:29:48,340
You have a guilty conscience?

640
00:29:48,660 --> 00:29:49,850
Keep your voice down!

641
00:29:49,850 --> 00:29:50,420
Shut up!

642
00:30:00,740 --> 00:30:01,560
Wu Dingyuan.

643
00:30:02,140 --> 00:30:03,890
Before I even reached adulthood,

644
00:30:03,890 --> 00:30:07,150
I had followed my grandfather
through countless battles.

645
00:30:07,230 --> 00:30:08,630
The people who died for me

646
00:30:10,900 --> 00:30:12,440
are simply too many.

647
00:30:13,970 --> 00:30:14,960
If you ask me

648
00:30:15,320 --> 00:30:17,060
to remember all their names,

649
00:30:18,710 --> 00:30:20,030
I really can't do it.

650
00:30:20,990 --> 00:30:23,010
But what I meant just now is that

651
00:30:24,450 --> 00:30:26,380
I haven't forgotten these people.

652
00:30:29,590 --> 00:30:30,870
As the Crown Prince,

653
00:30:33,070 --> 00:30:34,670
I've been hunted all the way,

654
00:30:35,620 --> 00:30:36,840
always on the run.

655
00:30:37,450 --> 00:30:38,560
Hunted, escaping,

656
00:30:38,580 --> 00:30:40,110
hunted and escaping again.

657
00:30:41,120 --> 00:30:43,180
If I can return to the capital safely,

658
00:30:44,460 --> 00:30:45,550
this will be

659
00:30:48,490 --> 00:30:50,070
all I can do in the end.

660
00:30:51,040 --> 00:30:52,080
I failed them.

661
00:31:01,660 --> 00:31:02,680
We're drunk.

662
00:31:03,340 --> 00:31:05,470
Why are we talking about this?

663
00:31:15,800 --> 00:31:16,660
Your Highness.

664
00:31:17,550 --> 00:31:18,510
What time is it?

665
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:21,780
Didn't I tell you

666
00:31:22,620 --> 00:31:23,950
to call me Young Master?

667
00:31:33,440 --> 00:31:34,240
Young Master.

668
00:31:34,970 --> 00:31:36,160
I was drunk just now.

669
00:31:36,290 --> 00:31:38,150
Please forgive me, Young Master.

670
00:31:38,230 --> 00:31:39,160
Little Xingren,

671
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:40,310
you misspoke.

672
00:31:40,810 --> 00:31:41,270
Sit.

673
00:31:41,600 --> 00:31:42,280
Sit, sit, sit.

674
00:31:42,280 --> 00:31:42,740
Come on.

675
00:31:48,180 --> 00:31:48,840
Old Mule.

676
00:31:49,990 --> 00:31:51,750
I'm not gonna sleep tonight.

677
00:31:51,960 --> 00:31:52,970
I'll drink with you.

678
00:31:52,970 --> 00:31:53,710
Tomorrow,

679
00:31:54,310 --> 00:31:55,030
we

680
00:31:55,530 --> 00:31:57,840
will go meet that Steward Wang.

681
00:31:57,960 --> 00:31:59,290
I want to see with my own eyes

682
00:31:59,290 --> 00:32:00,290
when you beat him.

683
00:32:00,990 --> 00:32:01,510
Come on.

684
00:32:01,990 --> 00:32:02,790
A toast to you.

685
00:32:03,140 --> 00:32:04,880
Stop drinking. You have business tomorrow.

686
00:32:04,880 --> 00:32:05,440
Drink up.

687
00:32:05,620 --> 00:32:06,960
No, no, no.

688
00:32:07,230 --> 00:32:08,940
Take it. You misspoke.

689
00:32:08,940 --> 00:32:09,940
So you must drink.

690
00:32:10,310 --> 00:32:11,620
Drink it on behalf of Young Master.

691
00:32:11,620 --> 00:32:12,140
I...

692
00:32:13,370 --> 00:32:14,170
Young Master.

693
00:32:15,460 --> 00:32:16,200
What Young Master?

694
00:32:16,200 --> 00:32:17,130
Hurry.

695
00:32:19,030 --> 00:32:19,430
Hurry.

696
00:32:19,450 --> 00:32:21,910
Drink less.
We have business to do tomorrow.

697
00:32:48,010 --> 00:32:50,650
[Countdown: 13 days]

698
00:33:02,620 --> 00:33:03,400
I am Wang Da,

699
00:33:03,990 --> 00:33:05,120
the steward here.

700
00:33:06,030 --> 00:33:08,510
I heard you were invincible yesterday,

701
00:33:08,770 --> 00:33:10,900
so I waited here specifically for you.

702
00:33:11,860 --> 00:33:13,120
How about this?

703
00:33:14,560 --> 00:33:16,220
One game to decide the winner.

704
00:33:34,140 --> 00:33:35,160
A little token of my appreciation.

705
00:33:35,160 --> 00:33:36,160
Please accept it.

706
00:33:36,300 --> 00:33:38,510
I hope you won't come back again.

707
00:33:38,960 --> 00:33:40,380
You're giving me money to chase me away?

708
00:33:40,380 --> 00:33:40,920
No.

709
00:33:41,210 --> 00:33:42,360
It's a parting gift.

710
00:33:44,280 --> 00:33:46,810
Cricket fighting
is not just about fighting.

711
00:33:47,480 --> 00:33:49,010
It's about making friends.

712
00:33:49,440 --> 00:33:50,120
I'm someone

713
00:33:50,950 --> 00:33:52,730
who values the word "friend."

714
00:33:53,860 --> 00:33:56,920
Our Young Master came here
because of your reputation.

715
00:34:00,610 --> 00:34:02,940
I wonder what I have done

716
00:34:03,140 --> 00:34:05,700
to deserve your special attention.

717
00:34:07,390 --> 00:34:10,510
Our Young Master wants to visit
a sick relative in the capital,

718
00:34:10,510 --> 00:34:11,960
but water levels
are low in the 5th month,

719
00:34:11,960 --> 00:34:13,489
so he can't travel quickly.

720
00:34:14,340 --> 00:34:15,440
Steward Wang,

721
00:34:15,719 --> 00:34:17,949
please consider
our Young Master's filial devotion

722
00:34:17,949 --> 00:34:20,010
and help arrange a letter of passage.

723
00:34:23,790 --> 00:34:26,190
This might be difficult for others,

724
00:34:27,239 --> 00:34:29,040
but it's really no trouble at all

725
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:31,449
for the Wang family.

726
00:34:33,420 --> 00:34:34,440
In that case,

727
00:34:35,020 --> 00:34:36,810
when do you plan to set off?

728
00:34:38,120 --> 00:34:39,600
The sooner, the better.

729
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:52,889
Young Master,

730
00:34:53,260 --> 00:34:55,190
we are not waiting for Wu Dingyuan?

731
00:34:56,400 --> 00:34:58,330
He'll find a way to catch up with us.

732
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:02,560
After you.

733
00:35:15,500 --> 00:35:21,480
♪ Behind grand gates, feasts never cease ♪

734
00:35:21,010 --> 00:35:21,760
My master

735
00:35:22,430 --> 00:35:24,360
has an estate here by the Han River.

736
00:35:24,760 --> 00:35:25,800
If you want the letter of passage,

737
00:35:25,070 --> 00:35:41,630
♪ By the river,
plain meals are hard to come by ♪

738
00:35:25,800 --> 00:35:27,320
you'll have to go there to collect it.

739
00:35:27,320 --> 00:35:29,050
Fortunately, it's quite close

740
00:35:29,150 --> 00:35:30,760
to the Yangzhou Pier.

741
00:35:30,970 --> 00:35:32,070
Once you have the letter,

742
00:35:32,070 --> 00:35:32,990
you can

743
00:35:33,300 --> 00:35:36,160
board the ship there first thing
tomorrow morning.

744
00:35:36,320 --> 00:35:37,720
Thank you, Steward Wang.

745
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:42,020
Do you have a carriage
waiting for you in Yangzhou?

746
00:35:42,670 --> 00:35:43,240
No.

747
00:35:43,150 --> 00:35:50,900
♪ In painted halls, silk robes shine ♪

748
00:35:43,650 --> 00:35:44,910
We are just passing by.

749
00:35:46,470 --> 00:35:48,000
Do you have any companions?

750
00:35:49,800 --> 00:35:51,190
There are a couple of...

751
00:35:50,930 --> 00:36:01,710
♪ On these shores, rags offer no warmth ♪

752
00:35:51,260 --> 00:35:54,010
A dozen or so fellow townsmen
are waiting for us at the inn.

753
00:35:54,010 --> 00:35:55,440
Once we get the letter,

754
00:35:55,650 --> 00:35:58,150
we'll need to go back and inform them.

755
00:35:59,470 --> 00:35:59,990
Yes.

756
00:36:07,700 --> 00:36:23,710
♪ In manicured gardens, pavilions abound ♪

757
00:36:08,740 --> 00:36:09,540
Steward Wang.

758
00:36:10,510 --> 00:36:13,110
I had no idea the estates here
were so enormous.

759
00:36:13,940 --> 00:36:14,800
This whole area

760
00:36:15,290 --> 00:36:17,740
is filled with private residences
owned by officials in Jinling.

761
00:36:17,740 --> 00:36:19,000
The Prefect of Jinling

762
00:36:19,170 --> 00:36:20,510
and the Commander of the Jinling Guard

763
00:36:20,510 --> 00:36:21,770
have properties here.

764
00:36:22,510 --> 00:36:24,960
Though the Qinhuai River
is right on their doorstep,

765
00:36:23,930 --> 00:36:41,910
♪ Who cares for the poor
with no roof over their heads? ♪

766
00:36:25,010 --> 00:36:26,170
they dare not indulge in its pleasures.

767
00:36:26,170 --> 00:36:28,670
They've been putting on a show

768
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:30,630
of being upright and incorruptible.

769
00:36:30,630 --> 00:36:33,550
But the moment
they get some time to themselves here,

770
00:36:33,550 --> 00:36:36,950
they let themselves go and indulge
to their hearts' content.

771
00:37:36,120 --> 00:37:38,310
We have distinguished guests tonight.

772
00:37:38,310 --> 00:37:39,690
The main entrance is too crowded,
with too many prying eyes.

773
00:37:39,690 --> 00:37:41,090
Let's take the side gate.

774
00:37:46,880 --> 00:37:47,740
Take them down!

775
00:37:58,330 --> 00:37:59,330
Hold him!

776
00:38:02,570 --> 00:38:03,370
Young Master!

777
00:38:10,340 --> 00:38:10,880
Come on!

778
00:38:11,320 --> 00:38:11,980
Who's next?

779
00:38:14,410 --> 00:38:16,710
What a gentleman,
caring nothing about money.

780
00:38:16,710 --> 00:38:18,240
The money I gave you to leave

781
00:38:18,370 --> 00:38:20,510
was more than enough
to buy 10 tribute vessels.

782
00:38:20,510 --> 00:38:22,880
With 10 vessels,
why do you need a letter of passage?

783
00:38:22,880 --> 00:38:23,440
Tell me.

784
00:38:23,910 --> 00:38:25,040
Who exactly are you?

785
00:38:25,510 --> 00:38:26,550
Let him go.

786
00:38:43,090 --> 00:38:43,750
Don't move!

787
00:38:53,060 --> 00:38:54,170
I'd like to see

788
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:56,280
how many shameful things are hidden

789
00:38:56,280 --> 00:38:58,760
under the facade of your Wang family.

790
00:38:59,590 --> 00:39:01,360
What?
Can't the Wang family afford to lose?

791
00:39:01,360 --> 00:39:02,670
Over this thousand-mile canal,

792
00:39:02,670 --> 00:39:05,730
are you the only one
who can arrange a letter of passage?

793
00:39:06,330 --> 00:39:08,630
You haven't answered my question yet, sir.

794
00:39:08,630 --> 00:39:09,440
Wang.

795
00:39:10,860 --> 00:39:12,410
Don't push it too far.

796
00:39:15,880 --> 00:39:17,300
You are either rich or noble.

797
00:39:17,300 --> 00:39:19,560
Anyone with eyes can see that at a glance.

798
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:20,760
Enough of that.

799
00:39:21,190 --> 00:39:22,450
Where is the promised letter of passage?

800
00:39:22,450 --> 00:39:23,780
Are you giving it or not?

801
00:39:25,220 --> 00:39:26,480
The letter of passage?

802
00:39:27,150 --> 00:39:28,350
I can't give it to you.

803
00:39:31,320 --> 00:39:32,030
Bastard!

804
00:39:32,780 --> 00:39:33,440
Watch them.

805
00:39:33,760 --> 00:39:34,900
Don't let them escape.

806
00:39:34,900 --> 00:39:36,070
-Yes!
-Yes!

807
00:40:03,640 --> 00:40:04,240
Come here.

808
00:40:05,850 --> 00:40:07,050
Hurry to the backyard

809
00:40:07,220 --> 00:40:08,950
and keep those men under watch.

810
00:40:09,720 --> 00:40:10,990
Keep your eyes peeled.

811
00:40:11,280 --> 00:40:12,950
You mustn't leave the woodshed unguarded.

812
00:40:12,950 --> 00:40:13,480
Hear me?

813
00:40:14,320 --> 00:40:14,980
-Yes!
-Yes!

814
00:40:15,320 --> 00:40:15,800
Yes!

815
00:40:24,110 --> 00:40:24,800
Be quiet.

816
00:40:25,260 --> 00:40:25,860
Follow me.

817
00:40:31,360 --> 00:40:31,960
Speak.

818
00:40:32,570 --> 00:40:34,400
Where is that young master?

819
00:40:35,740 --> 00:40:37,030
You wouldn't dare kill me.

820
00:40:37,030 --> 00:40:39,690
If you do,
none of you will leave this place alive.

821
00:40:39,690 --> 00:40:40,890
My life is worthless.

822
00:40:41,010 --> 00:40:42,900
But yours is worth far more than mine.

823
00:40:42,900 --> 00:40:43,960
A life for a life.

824
00:40:44,070 --> 00:40:45,000
I won't lose out.

825
00:40:46,700 --> 00:40:49,430
Your life and that bookworm's
aren't worth much.

826
00:40:49,460 --> 00:40:51,180
But do you dare say
that young master's life is worthless too?

827
00:40:51,180 --> 00:40:52,300
Cut the crap.

828
00:40:52,700 --> 00:40:53,500
Take me to him.

829
00:40:53,500 --> 00:40:54,100
Which way?

830
00:41:04,510 --> 00:41:05,010
Come on!

831
00:41:05,150 --> 00:41:05,800
Stop!

832
00:41:07,150 --> 00:41:07,920
Stop!

833
00:41:10,240 --> 00:41:11,150
Tell your men

834
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:12,860
to put down their weapons.

835
00:41:13,210 --> 00:41:14,010
Put them down.

836
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:15,630
Put them down!

837
00:41:15,630 --> 00:41:16,340
Hurry up!

838
00:41:16,720 --> 00:41:17,520
Put them down!

839
00:41:19,240 --> 00:41:20,990
What's that room used for?

840
00:41:22,490 --> 00:41:23,490
Th-the woodshed.

841
00:41:24,170 --> 00:41:25,540
Get them all inside.

842
00:41:26,370 --> 00:41:27,370
All of you, get in.

843
00:41:27,920 --> 00:41:28,590
Hurry up!

844
00:41:30,670 --> 00:41:31,150
Move!

845
00:41:39,490 --> 00:41:40,490
Behave yourself.

846
00:41:41,240 --> 00:41:42,640
Tell them to crouch down!

847
00:41:44,190 --> 00:41:44,990
Lock the door.

848
00:41:51,470 --> 00:41:52,130
Don't move!

849
00:41:54,010 --> 00:41:54,810
Young Master,

850
00:41:55,110 --> 00:41:57,340
it's not that
I don't want to go get my master,

851
00:41:57,340 --> 00:41:59,540
but your friend is really too ruthless.

852
00:42:00,590 --> 00:42:02,320
Still, I'll be honest with you.

853
00:42:02,650 --> 00:42:03,980
Even if my master comes,

854
00:42:04,360 --> 00:42:05,880
the letter of passage you want

855
00:42:05,880 --> 00:42:07,140
won't be so easy to get!

856
00:42:08,050 --> 00:42:09,250
Then name your terms.

857
00:42:09,850 --> 00:42:10,980
Good-for-Nothing.

858
00:42:19,070 --> 00:42:19,870
Young Master.

859
00:42:20,720 --> 00:42:22,020
As long as we can get the letter,

860
00:42:22,020 --> 00:42:24,150
I think we should avoid making a scene.

861
00:42:24,650 --> 00:42:26,380
We don't want any more trouble.

862
00:42:28,220 --> 00:42:29,150
Little Xingren!

863
00:42:31,360 --> 00:42:32,020
Keep going.

864
00:42:33,690 --> 00:42:34,110
I...

865
00:42:34,360 --> 00:42:35,030
No, no, no!

866
00:42:35,230 --> 00:42:36,290
Don't do this!

867
00:42:45,530 --> 00:42:46,070
You.

868
00:42:46,900 --> 00:42:47,470
You!

869
00:42:47,830 --> 00:42:48,430
Come here.

870
00:42:52,640 --> 00:42:54,300
Tie everyone's hands.

871
00:42:55,290 --> 00:42:55,850
I...

872
00:43:00,400 --> 00:43:01,360
I will

873
00:43:02,420 --> 00:43:03,480
only ask this once.

874
00:43:05,630 --> 00:43:07,360
Where's the letter of passage?

875
00:43:07,530 --> 00:43:08,500
It's in the study.

876
00:43:08,500 --> 00:43:09,910
Where's the study?
